<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport Jan-June.</title>
<headline>ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport Jan-June.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-June 1996, compared to the same period last year, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The airport handled 915,057 tonnes of cargo in the period in question, up 8.7 percent on January-June 1995.</p>
<p>Los Angeles airport was second-place in the ACI table of top cargo-handling airports was as a result of reporting 821,149 tonnes, up 9.0 percent on the previous year's levels.</p>
<p>In third place was Miami, which handled 815,585 tonnes, an increase of 6.7 percent on the first six months of 1995.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in January-June 1996, with the volume they handled, the percentage change over January-June 1995 and, in parentheses, their January-June 1995 ranking, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  (1)  Memphis	    915,057 tonnes  up   8.7 pct</p>
<p> 2  (5)  Los Angeles	821,149 tonnes  up   9.0</p>
<p> 3  (3)  Miami		815,585 tonnes  up   6.7</p>
<p> 4  (4)  New York	   779,544 tonnes  up   1.4</p>
<p> 5  (2)  Tokyo		771,045 tonnes  down 5.5</p>
<p> 6  (6)  Frankfurt	  716,824 tonnes  up   2.0</p>
<p> 7  (7)  Hong Kong	  716,824 tonnes  up   5.0</p>
<p> 8  (8)  Louisville	 677,603 tonnes  up   2.4</p>
<p> 9  (10) Seoul		620,958 tonnes  up   9.1</p>
<p> 10 (16) Anchorage	  620,958 tonnes  up  42.4</p>
<p> 11 (9)  Chicago	    592,061 tonnes  down 0.8</p>
<p> 12 (12) Singapore	  570,760 tonnes  up   5.5</p>
<p> 13 (11) London Heathrow  556,611 tonnes  up   1.4</p>
<p> 14 (13) Amsterdam	  550,315 tonnes  up  11.6</p>
<p> 15 (15) Paris-CDG	  470,881 tonnes  up   2.2</p>
<p> 16 (14) New York Newark  470,192 tonnes	 0.0</p>
<p> 17 (17) Atlanta	    389,678 tonnes  up   1.8</p>
<p> 18 (18) Dallas F/Worth   372,833 tonnes  down 1.0</p>
<p> 19 (19) Taipei	     364,108 tonnes  down 1.5</p>
<p> 20 (-)  Dayton	     354,558 tonnes  up  15.5</p>
